# Local env files must never ship to Vercel.
#
# The Vercel CLI does NOT honour .gitignore when uploading, so `vercel --prod`
# was bundling .env into the deployment. Next then loads it at runtime, where it
# fills in any var Vercel itself doesn't define — which silently forced
# INNGEST_DEV=1 in production and pinned the whole app to Inngest dev mode
# (has_signing_key: true, but mode: "dev", and no workflow ever ran).
#
# Production env lives in the Vercel project settings. Nowhere else.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
